    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "It quadruples (increases by a factor of 4).",
      "worked": "Doubling the diameter doubles the radius. Since $A=\\pi r^2$, the new area is $\\pi(2r)^2=4\\pi r^2$, four times the original area.",
